      "writtenOn": "2018-01-16T21:15:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looks like spawn* methods modify the state of the lineage. If so, why do we need a Builder pattern? Why not start with an empty lineage an offer a way to parse from encoded form?\n\nConsider going with immutable lineage objects. There, these spawn* methods would return a new modified instance of lineage as their result. Alternatively, you could expose spawn* methodsin the Builder. The pattern in that case is that lineage instances have a buildUpon() or builder() method which returns a Builder initialized to the state of the current lineage, and the Builder can then modify this state (without modifying the original lineage) and return a new potentially modified lineage.",
      "revId": "c087ae0246d84e0838df0edfcd59f913f1e17558",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
